# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REACT_APP_WORLD_CDN
#
# OPTIONAL. Root URL of a CDN bucket serving the scroll-cinematic media
# assets (poster images and video clips under public/world/).
#
# By default you do not need this. The media is committed to the repo and
# served same-origin, so a fresh clone works with no configuration at all.
# Set this only if you later want to move the media off the repo and onto
# a CDN, which keeps clones light and gives video proper edge delivery.
#
# Create React App inlines all REACT_APP_* variables at BUILD time, not
# at runtime. Changing this value requires a rebuild and redeploy. The
# value ends up in the compiled bundle, which is fine because these are
# publicly accessible assets.
#
# When unset or empty the app uses same-origin paths (/world/...) and the
# engine's blob load path. When set, the engine switches to assigning the
# URL straight to video.src, which needs no CORS on the bucket but does
# need it to honour HTTP range requests.
#
# Cloudflare R2 example:
# REACT_APP_WORLD_CDN=https://pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.r2.dev
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REACT_APP_WORLD_CDN=https://pub-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.r2.dev
